{"hypotheses":[
  {"statement":"Beverage revenue is high primarily because a small number of drink products generate most of the revenue (concentration effect), not broad-based demand across the drink menu.","priorConfidence":0.55,"target":"beverage_revenue_by_product","action":"breakdown","expectation":"A small subset (e.g., top 2-3) of product_name entries account for a disproportionately large share (e.g., >60%) of beverage_revenue_by_product; if revenue is evenly spread across many products, this is refuted."},

  {"statement":"Beverage revenue is high because drink order volume (orders.drink_orders) has grown, not because of higher prices per drink order.","priorConfidence":0.5,"target":"orders.drink_orders","action":"compare_time","expectation":"orders.drink_orders shows a rising trend over recent periods that tracks with order_item.drink_revenue growth; if drink order counts are flat while revenue rises, this is refuted (pointing to price/mix instead)."},

  {"statement":"Beverage revenue is disproportionately driven by one customer_type segment (e.g., returning customers) rather than being evenly distributed across new and existing customers.","priorConfidence":0.5,"target":"customer_profile","action":"breakdown","expectation":"customer_profile broken out by customers.customer_type shows one segment contributing a clear majority of beverage-related revenue/orders; if segments contribute roughly proportionally to their size, this is refuted."},

  {"statement":"Beverage revenue is high because it is concentrated among a small set of top spending customers rather than broad customer adoption of drinks.","priorConfidence":0.45,"target":"top_beverage_customers","action":"lookup_block","expectation":"The top_beverage_customers list shows a steep drop-off, with the top few customers accounting for a large share of beverage revenue; if spend is spread evenly across many customers, this is refuted."},

  {"statement":"The high level of beverage revenue reflects an ongoing upward trend (momentum), not a one-time spike, as shown by rising drink revenue share of total revenue over recent months.","priorConfidence":0.4,"target":"order_item.drink_revenue_pct","action":"compare_time","expectation":"order_item.drink_revenue_pct increases steadily month-over-month (consistent with order_item.revenue_growth_mom being positive for drinks); if the percentage is flat or was already high long ago with no recent increase, this is refuted."}
]}
